  "script": "What would happen if you tried to jump from New York to London? The world long jump record is 8.95 meters. Mike Powell, 1991. So you land in Times Square, about 9 meters from where you started. A guy dressed as Elmo claps. So you build a ramp off the top of the Empire State Building. 381 meters up. To make it, you need to leave at about 26,000 kilometers an hour. That's over 20 times the speed of sound. Your arc tops out around 1,400 kilometers up. More than 3 times higher than the Space Station. Somewhere over the Atlantic, you pass a cruise ship. 3,000 people film it. Nobody believes them. You come down over London about 18 minutes after take-off. Before you even touch the ground, it starts raining. And honestly? The flight would have been cheaper.",
